    ``where``. It can either have same dimension as input

    >>> where=jnp.array([[0, 0, 1, 0],
    ...                  [0, 0, 1, 1],
    ...                  [1, 1, 1, 0]], dtype=bool)
    >>> jnp.nanmin(x, axis=1, keepdims=True, initial=0, where=where)
    Array([[ 0.],
           [-4.],
           [ 0.]], dtype=float32)

